[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glassops-platform/glassops/pulls/46","id":5061040815,"node_id":"PR_kwDORCCdv88AAAABLalarw","html_url":"https://github.com/glassops-platform/glassops/pull/46","diff_url":"https://github.com/glassops-platform/glassops/pull/46.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/glassops-platform/glassops/pull/46.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glassops-platform/glassops/issues/46","number":46,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: Salesforce login, org guard, describe, plan and check-only validate","user":{"login":"rdbumstead","id":44008640,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MDA4NjQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44008640?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdbumstead","html_url":"https://github.com/rdbumstead","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdbumstead/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdbumstead/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdbumstead/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdbumstead/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdbumstead/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdbumstead/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdbumstead/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdbumstead/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdbumstead/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What this does\n\nThis adds the Salesforce read side to the `glassops` CLI. It can now log in to an org, prove the org is the one the config names, work out a change set and run a check-only validate.\n\n- `glassops describe --target T` logs in, runs the org Id and tier guard, and records what the org reports.\n- `glassops doctor --auth` logs in to each target and runs the guard. Plain `doctor` still never logs in.\n- `glassops plan` works out the change set between two git refs with `sfdx-git-delta`, or lists the whole source when deltas are off.\n- `glassops validate --target T` runs a check-only validate of that change set, with an optional fallback target.\n\n## How it works\n\n**Logins.** Each command logs in for itself in a private temporary home, with `HOME` and `USERPROFILE` pointed at it. The key file and the Salesforce CLI's state live there and nowhere else, so nothing reaches the logins already on the machine. The directory is removed when the command ends, when the login fails, and on Ctrl+C or SIGTERM. Secrets never appear as command arguments. Logins are retried only on network and server errors, never on a bad key, an unknown user or an expired token.\n\n**The guard.** After every login, the org's Id is compared with the config on its first 15 characters, case-sensitively. `prod` and `devhub` targets must be production orgs, and `ephemeral` targets must be scratch orgs. A mismatch exits 2 before anything else runs.\n\n**Validate is check-only by construction.** It only runs `sf project deploy validate`, and it reads the full result from `sf project deploy report`. A failed validate's own JSON holds nothing but the deploy Id. If either result reports anything other than check-only, the command exits 2.\n\n**Nothing private in results or logs.** The org's company name is never read, usernames are masked, and email-shaped text in tool errors is masked too.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Every parser is tested against real `sf` and `sfdx-git-delta` output captured from a Dev Hub and a scratch org, then scrubbed. That includes five real login failures and the thin JSON a failed validate returns.\n- Signal cleanup is tested with a helper process that receives SIGTERM.\n- `testdata/sfdx/` holds a small project whose two commits change a class, edit a permission set and delete a field.\n- I ran the whole end-to-end flow locally in the image against my Dev Hub and a scratch org: `doctor --auth`, a forced guard mismatch, `describe`, both kinds of plan, the check-only validate and the cleanup.\n- The new `cli-e2e.yml` workflow does the same in CI. It runs on demand and on pushes to `main`, not on every PR, because a Developer Edition Dev Hub allows three active scratch orgs.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Scratch orgs cannot be reached by JWT through an external client app. The workflow signs the org up with a `ScratchOrgInfo` record and exchanges its auth code instead. `sf org create scratch` is avoided because it leaves a live org behind when its own follow-up login fails.\n- A check-only validate of a delta that deletes something fails in a fresh scratch org, because the org never had the base branch's state. The workflow checks the delta's facts and validates the full source.\n- The workflow has a temporary trigger for this branch, which comes out before merge.\n","created_at":"2026-10-29T02:28:00Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T02:42:41Z","closed_at":"2026-10-29T02:41:38Z","merged_at":"2026-10-29T02:41:37Z","merge_commit_sha":"20459158b4f16da4cddc816ac7c1d695177af196","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glassops-platform/glassops/pulls/46/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glassops-platform/glassops/pulls/46/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glassops-platform/glassops/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glassops-platform/glassops/issues/46/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/glassops-platform/glassops/statuses/bbc53dc8eec52617b0e14ab10a771897cde836e7","head":{"label":"glassops-platform:feat/phase2-salesforce-read","ref":"feat/phase2-salesforce-read","sha":"bbc53dc8eec52617b0e14ab10a771897cde836e7","user":{"login":"glassops-platform","id":255719674,"node_id":"O_kgDODz34-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/255719674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/glasso